[
  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186176053,
      "id": "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326",
      "title": "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "b39f1a26-af7a-5fd3-b7d9-2fa382bc016c",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\csc x$?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The range is all real numbers.\n- **II.** The graph does not intersect the $y$-axis.\n- **III.** The function has no global minimum or maximum.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "3f2ca583-f967-594b-a2e2-daf15c919d20",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "5d7fcce2-8ed2-5d9b-bd74-a9ff620d2360",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "526c50b3-beb9-59ae-8d32-1d74b9c27d18",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "5d7fcce2-8ed2-5d9b-bd74-a9ff620d2360"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "cddd997b-d915-554f-ada4-074d6c5a4dd3",
          ":answer-field/key": "II",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "46187b3d-a8a0-5e46-8aa1-0744ffa059fe",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "a06b4390-6b52-5ed9-874d-1c6e93e4fa75",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "a06b4390-6b52-5ed9-874d-1c6e93e4fa75"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "f22f6d76-facb-575e-b4c0-35505f62cfa1",
          ":answer-field/key": "III",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "ed215f5f-d18f-59b3-98dc-3ebb8152ebd5",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "e6a63691-d789-5720-9a9e-c40a5ba17930",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "e6a63691-d789-5720-9a9e-c40a5ba17930"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\csc x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty,-1]\\cup[1,\\infty)$.  Hence, statement I is false.\n\n- The graph does not intersect the $y$-axis, as $x=0$ is not in the domain. Hence, statement II is true.\n\n- The range is unbounded above and below, so the function has no global minimum or maximum. Hence, statement III is true.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy"
    },
